--- body ---
## Context
Audit: `conception/2026-10-29-memory-system-audit.md` (PR #1984) §4.3, R4 and R5. Claude Code loads its native auto-memory (28 notes, 4.2 KB index) in every
session; none of it passes through roar, hoard or review, several notes are rules in substance,
and one says it disagrees with `rules/git.md`. The repository index is no longer injected at
start (`tests/test_on_start_memory_injection.py`), and the repository store is not read (1346).

## Scope
Decide from 1346's numbers, then implement one of:
- a. native auto-memory off for the harness, and roar journals what the author dictates;
- b. keep it, and each hoard lists the native notes for the author to promote or delete;
- c. restore an index in Claude Code's start context, or point `autoMemoryDirectory` at the repo.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] The author's choice is recorded with its rationale
- [ ] The chosen path is implemented and measured once with the 1346 census
